Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:53:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] A lesson that ends asks for its draft

lesson_end now asks lesson-finalize, the database's door: it merges the
room's segments with Daily's stored transcript (with the family's
transcript consent), computes the lesson's metrics, and with the family's
ai_analysis consent runs three Claude passes ported from the room's own
modules (coaching feedback, follow-ups under the centre's rules, the
report draft in the form's exact vocabulary), falling back to the
heuristic per pass rather than losing the run. Everything lands through
worker_store_lesson_results; a lesson older than a day stores quietly.
A project that cannot ask still closes the lesson and says so on the
lesson's log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
